remstart
    QUESTS 2.0: THE QUEST BOARD
    an experiment (Chris, 2026-11-09), and since 2026-11-11 the quests of the game, in place of the ones of
    fish_headers_quests. those come back only while the FISH_QUEST1 environment variable is set, and then nothing in
    here does anything. the tests of the old quests turn this off (fishBoard).

    a quest is a puzzle of its own, on a board of its own. taking it turns the board over, the way that a flip
    of the ladder does (THE SPIN in fish_headers_extinct), but all of it, and the quest's board is on the other
    side. leaving turns it back, and the game's board is there again, exactly as it was.

    THE GAME WAITS. nothing on the game's board changes while the quest is played: its fish, its coral, its ink,
    the moon, the score, the count of moves, the multiplier, the cards. the quest board does not count moves or
    score points for the game. so everything that the quest board could change is kept when it turns over
    (qbKeep), and put back when it turns back (qbGiveBack).

    ONLY WHAT THE PUZZLE GIVES. the cards stay with the game's board. while the quest board is up, no card has
    been taken: their uses are kept and set to 0, and the moves come out of their slots. so a bomb on the
    game's board is not on the quest board.

    THE QUEST BOARD is a little board, the way that the boards of the tutorial and of Ava's puzzles are
    (TUTORIAL_BOARD): a gap is a cell with no fish, nothing comes in to fill a column, and the fish fall
    (QB_ON goes with PUZZLE_ON wherever that makes the fish of a puzzle fall and keeps the game's other
    systems out of it). it is the same size as the game's board, so that it can turn over in its place.

    TAKING AND LEAVING. the pickup of the quest is in the stack, off the right of the board (THE STACK). swapping it
    down onto the check mark opens its talk, and taking it there turns the board over to the quest. on the quest
    board, it is still out there, and
    swapping it up onto the X turns the board back. the quest is waiting at its pickup again, to be taken, and its
    puzzle starts from the beginning when it is.
remend

global QUEST2_ON = 0 `1 unless FISH_QUEST1 is set. see setup_qboard.

` where the turning over has got to: 0 the game's board is up, 1 it is turning to the quest, 2 the quest board is up,
` 3 it is turning back
global QB_PHASE = 0
global QB_ON = 0 `1 while the fish on the board are the quest's. it changes halfway through a turn, while the board is edge on.
global QB_QUEST = 0 `the quest whose board it is
global QB_SPIN_MS = -1 `when the turn started, or -1
global QB_SPIN_TIME = 900 `how long a turn takes, in milliseconds
global QB_SPIN_SWAPPED = 0 `1 once the board has changed sides, halfway through
global QB_START_CELL = -1 `where the cursor goes on the quest board

` WHAT IS KEPT. the board, cell by cell
