remstart
    THE PUZZLES ARE MADE AS THE GAME GOES (Chris, 2026-11-09: a quest at a level must not be the same in every game).
    a puzzle is made from the seed of the game, the quest and its level, on a random stream of its own (QB_RNG), so
    the same game always gets the same puzzle and the game's own streams are never touched. it is made backwards
    from its answer, and then played forwards to check it, the way that build/make_puzzle_boards.py makes Ava's:

    - it starts from the board that is left at the end, a few fish that make no group.
    - for every swap of the answer, from the last back to the first, it puts the group that the swap pops back on
      the board (a line of three, across or up and down, pushing the fish over it up), and then swaps one of its
      fish with a fish next to it, so that the group is broken up until the swap puts it together again.
    - nothing on the board may make a group before a swap, because it would pop on its own.
    - then the answer is played forwards on a copy, with every pop, fall and pop after a fall, and the puzzle is
      only taken when every swap pops something and every egg pops on the swap that it has to. otherwise it is
      thrown away, and the next one is tried.

    so every puzzle can be done, and the player may well find another way.

    EVERY SWAP POPS. on the quest board, as on Ava's, a swap that would pop nothing is not made (puzzleBlocksSwap).
    otherwise the count of an egg could be run down with swaps that do nothing.

    HATCH. some of the fish are eggs, with a count on them. every swap takes one off of every egg's count. an egg
    has to pop on the swap that takes its count to 0: before that it breaks, and if it is still there after that,
    it has hatched without the player. either way the puzzle is lost, and the move keys take swaps back (the first
    one) or start the puzzle over (the second one). every egg hatched finishes the quest.
remend
global QB_RNG = 8 `the random stream that the puzzles are made from. see RandomCommands.cs: there are 16.
global QB_W = 9 `the size of the quest board
global QB_H = 6
global QB_LEVEL = 1
global dim QB_LEVEL_OF(40) `the level that every quest is at, in this game. a quest goes up a level when it is done.

` the puzzle as it is made: kinds, and eggs, cell by cell, from the top left, QB_W across
global dim QB_G(400)
